  "default_direction": "en_to_pl",
  "note": "B1 liść -- 'the vocab that makes the virile units worth having' (B1-SPINE.md). Five new profession pairs (m/f), all checked against check_new.py as brand new: policjant/policjantka, informatyk/informatyczka, kucharz/kucharka, dziennikarz/dziennikarka, turysta/turystka -- picked specifically so every masculine noun falls inside the REGULAR virile-nom rule already taught (policjant/turysta = -t stem, like pacjent/artysta; informatyk = -k stem, like Polak/rolnik; kucharz/dziennikarz = already-soft rz stem, like lekarz), so producing the plural here is applying an owned rule to new lemmas, not teaching a new one. Feminine plurals (policjantki, informatyczki, kucharki, dziennikarki, turystki) apply the ALREADY-taught a2_plural_nom hard-stem -i-after-k/g rule -- also not new grammar, just new lemmas on an owned pattern. Plus ludzie ('people'), the suppletive plural of czlowiek, handed over WHOLE as a closed vocabulary item -- deliberately NOT derived (czlowiek->ludzie is a true irregular, explicitly fenced from the b1_virile_nom production rule in that pack's own note) but valuable enough as the single highest-frequency virile-agreement noun in the language that leaving it out of the one B1 unit literally named 'Ludzie' would be the more conservative-in-name-only choice. Logged: dzieci (children) was considered as a second whole-form irregular for contrast -- Polish famously treats dzieci as grammatically NON-virile despite meaning people -- and dropped. It is already fenced in the plural_nom catalogue entry as a suppletive, b1_virile_reco's own note explicitly declined to use it for exactly this reason, and stacking a second irregular exception in the same pack as ludzie adds a real chance of the two suppletives blurring together for an absolute beginner with no payoff the spine actually asked for. Every sentence gives exactly one new form per frame: base nouns are anchored in the word list (matching the grammar-pack convention where match/blocks introduce raw pairs before combination), and every Zdanie combines a plural form with only already-taught structures -- byc_present (sa), the new-this-block past_plural verb pracowali/pracowaly (from b1_virile_past, reused here rather than re-taught), mieszkali/mieszkaly and byli (a2_past_plural / b1_virile_past), and the locatives w banku / w firmie / w miescie / w parku, all confirmed taught via check_new.py (w restauracji and w kuchni were checked and are NOT taught anywhere yet, so neither appears in this file). No adjective virile form beyond the already-taught 'dobrzy' (recalled once, in predicate position only, exactly as the two grammar units before this one always used it) is asked for or shown.",
